  "docTitle": "Bitmask DP - SDE Prep Dojo",
  "description": "Bitmask DP deep dive for n <= 20: subsets as integers, lowest-bit and submask iteration tricks (3^n), partition into k equal-sum subsets, shortest path visiting all nodes (BFS over node and mask, Held-Karp), assignment DP by popcount and submask DP for splitting items among k people, with steppers and Go, C++, Java and Python templates.",
  "hero": {
    "tag": "header",
    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\r\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\"><span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"5\">Level 5 - Interview-ready</span><span class=\"time\">40 min</span><span class=\"chip\">Deep dive</span><span class=\"chip\">Dynamic programming</span><span class=\"chip\">n &lt;= 20</span></div>\r\n  <h1>Bitmask DP</h1>\r\n  <p class=\"lead\">When a problem has at most about 20 items and the answer depends on <i>which</i> items are already used, store that set as the bits of one integer and run DP over all 2<sup>n</sup> sets. This page covers the mask tricks (lowest bit, popcount, submask walk), partition into k equal-sum subsets, the shortest path that visits every node, the assignment problem, and splitting items among k people with submask DP. Templates in Go, C++, Java and Python.</p>\r\n"
  },
